# The Alliance Paladin weapon chain: The Tome of Valor (1793 from Duthorian
# Rall for Humans, 1794 from Tiza Battleforge for Dwarves; they close each
# other; then 1649 from the book, 1650, 1651 the defense of Daphne Stilwell,
# 1652: Bastion of Stormwind and Sense Undead) and The Test of Righteousness
# (1653, 1654, 1806: Jordan Stilwell outside Ironforge forges Verigan's Fist
# from four parts), with Bailor's Ore Shipment (1655) and Seeking the Kor Gem
# (1442) for two of the parts.
# Sources: Forever's quest data (quests.json, the knowledge base) for givers,
# enders, objectives, droppers, drop rates and mob levels (Goblin Woodcarvers
# level 18-19 elite, 13 spawns, the lumber every kill; 15 elite Mo'grosh
# Ogres at 18-19, five-minute respawn; Blackfathom naga 20-24 elite, the gem
# one in two; Defias Raiders 17-18); the Forever server tables for the
# rewards (1652 teaches Sense Undead, spell 5503, and gives Bastion of
# Stormwind; 1806 gives Verigan's Fist); players' notes in Forever's quest
# data for the waves (three, four, then five raiders; you or Daphne dying
# fails it), the path to Daphne beside the Deadmines' back exit, Bailor
# downstairs in Thelsamar, the ore box by a big tree and a broken wagon, the
# hammer on a crate across from the horses in Shadowfang Keep's stables, the
# Kor Gem only dropping while you hold Thundris's quest and not in a raid
# group. Warcraft Wiki, "Paladin quests", agrees on the parts' places.
# Dungeon entrances from dungeons.json (DungeonJournal, live map frame).
# Three parts are group work: the Deadmines and Shadowfang Keep (groups of
# five) and the elite naga at Blackfathom Deeps; the Mo'grosh ogres are
# elite too. The parts can be gathered in any order once Jordan has given you
# The Test of Righteousness; Bailor's and Thundris's quests open only then.
# Forsaken paladins have their own level 20 weapon chain, the Moonsilver
# Blade (forever/class/paladin/lumina-windsinger).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Tome of Valor

step The Tome of Valor (Ironforge)
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  tip At 20 Tiza Battleforge, upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries in the Mystic Ward, gives you the Tome of Valor. Right-click it: it sends you to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. Take the Deeprun Tram from Ironforge to Stormwind.
  level 20
  turnin 1794 direct                  -- Tiza Battleforge

step The Tome of Valor
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Duthorian Rall stands in the Cathedral of Light. Humans get the Tome of Valor from him. Right-click the book to start its quest and hand it straight back to him.
  level 20
  turnin 1793 direct only Human       -- Duthorian Rall
  accept 1649 item 6776               -- Right-click the Tome of Valor
  turnin 1649                         -- Duthorian Rall
  accept 1650

step Daphne Stilwell
  zone Westfall
  tip Daphne Stilwell's farmhouse stands on the south-west coast of Westfall, south of Moonbrook: take the path that runs south beside the Deadmines' back exit. When you take her quest, she walks from her orchard to the house and three waves of Defias Raiders (level 17-18) attack: three, then four, then five. Fight close to her so they do not swarm her, and heal her when she drops. You get time to eat and drink between waves, and she heals to full. If you or Daphne die, the quest fails: abandon it and take it again from her (she is back five minutes after dying). Players find it hard alone before about 24.
  turnin 1650                         -- Daphne Stilwell
  accept 1651
  complete 1651                       -- Protect Daphne Stilwell: three waves
  turnin 1651
  accept 1652

step Duthorian Rall
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Back to the Cathedral of Light: Duthorian gives you the Bastion of Stormwind shield and teaches you Sense Undead.
  turnin 1652 reward 9607             -- Duthorian Rall: Bastion of Stormwind, Sense Undead
  accept 1653

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Test of Righteousness

step Jordan Stilwell
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip Jordan Stilwell works outside the gates of Ironforge, not inside. He gives you Jordan's Weapon Notes: four parts, in any order. Keep the notes.
  turnin 1653                         -- Jordan Stilwell
  accept 1654

step Bailor Stonehand
  zone Loch Modan
  tip Bailor Stonehand is downstairs in the house of Thelsamar that has a tailoring merchant outside. His quest only opens once you hold Jordan's.
  accept 1655                         -- Bailor Stonehand

step Bailor's Ore
  zone Loch Modan
  tip The crate of ore sits outdoors in the middle of the Mo'grosh ogre camp in north-east Loch Modan, beside a big tree and a broken wagon, between the caves. The camp holds about fifteen Mo'grosh ogres, elite (level 18-19), who knock you down and come back after five minutes: grouping up is encouraged; at 20-22 it needs a group of about three. The crate is back two seconds after each loot, so every paladin in the group gets one.
  collect 6992 quest 1655.1           -- Bailor's Ore crate

step Back to Bailor
  zone Loch Modan
  tip Bailor turns the ore into Jordan's Refined Ore Shipment, the part Jordan wants.
  turnin 1655 reward 6993             -- Bailor Stonehand
  collect 6993 quest 1654.2

step Whitestone Oak Lumber
  zone Westfall
  tip The Deadmines is a group of five under Moonbrook; the instance portal is at the bottom of the Moonbrook mine. The Goblin Woodcarvers (elite, level 18-19) in the mast room with Sneed drop the lumber every time.
  goto 42.5,71.7 live "The Deadmines, in the Moonbrook mine"
  collect 6994 quest 1654.1 @42.5,71.7 live -- Goblin Woodcarvers, inside

step Jordan's Smithing Hammer
  zone Silverpine Forest
  tip Shadowfang Keep is a dungeon for a group of five in the low to mid 20s, in southern Silverpine Forest, Horde land: a long trip for the Alliance, through the Wetlands, Arathi and Hillsbrad. The hammer lies on a crate across from the horses in the stables, early in the dungeon, at the far end of the courtyard before the ramp up; it is back five minutes after someone takes it.
  goto 44.8,67.8 live "Shadowfang Keep"
  collect 6895 quest 1654.3 @44.8,67.8 live -- Jordan's Hammer, inside

step Thundris Windweaver
  zone Darkshore
  tip Thundris Windweaver is in Auberdine. Take his quest before you hunt naga: the Kor Gem never drops without it.
  accept 1442                         -- Thundris Windweaver

step The Corrupted Kor Gem
  zone Ashenvale
  tip The Blackfathom naga in the flooded passages around the Blackfathom Deeps entrance, on Ashenvale's north-west coast, drop the Corrupted Kor Gem: Tide Priestesses (level 20-21), Oracles (21-22) and Sea Witches (23-24), one in two. You do not need to enter the instance. All are elite: grouping up is encouraged; players solo them one at a time, with difficulty. They heal themselves, run for help at low health, satyrs stand near some, and the Sea Witches cast Frost Nova up close. Some players report no drop while in a raid group.
  collect 6995 quest 1442.1

step The Purified Kor Gem
  zone Darkshore
  tip Back to Thundris in Auberdine: he purifies the gem.
  turnin 1442 reward 7083             -- Thundris Windweaver
  collect 7083 quest 1654.4

step Verigan's Fist
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip Bring the four parts to Jordan Stilwell outside Ironforge. Accept his last quest and wait by him while he forges the mace at his anvil.
  turnin 1654                         -- Jordan Stilwell
  accept 1806
  turnin 1806 reward 6953             -- Verigan's Fist
